An adversary uses path manipulation to access files and directories outside the intended directory. By using ../ sequences or absolute paths, attackers can read sensitive system files.

Mitigation:
Attack Flow: Attacker sends path with ../../etc/passwd → application uses path in file operation → sensitive file is read/written
Defense: Use path.resolve() and verify the result is within the allowed directory.

Examples:
// Attack: filename = "../../../etc/passwd"
fs.readFile("./uploads/" + filename); // Reads /etc/passwd
// Defense:
const safe = path.resolve(uploadsDir, filename);
if (!safe.startsWith(uploadsDir)) throw new Error("Path traversal");

