An attacker submits duplicate HTTP parameters to cause the web application to interpret them in unexpected ways, potentially bypassing validation or WAF rules.

Mitigation:
Attack Flow: Attacker sends duplicate parameters (?id=1&id=2) → server and application may handle differently → validation bypass possible
Defense: Explicitly select first/last parameter value. Use strict parameter parsing.

Examples:
